शामन, अस्, m. one who ‘settles’ or destroys,
N. of Yama (= शमन); (अम्), n. conciliation;
tranquillity, peace; settling, killing, slaughter; end,
(शामनं या, to go to an end, be destroyed);
(ई), f. the southern quarter.

समना, ind. Ved. in battle, (Sāy. = समने);
(according to others समना is an old inst. = सम्-
आनया fr. 2. समान, see Nirukta

सामन् सामन्, अ, n. (probably to be con-
nected with rt. शम्, see शामन्, cf. rt. साम्, col. 1;
in Uṇādi-s.

सम्-मति, इस्, f. sameness of opinion, agreement,
consent, assent, approval, approbation; wish, desire;
esteem, respect, homage; regard, affection, love;
self-knowledge; order, command.

समद् 2. समद्, त्, f. (in the Pada स-मद्;
according to Yāska either fr. 1. सम्-अद् above or
सम्-मद्), Ved. a battle, contest, fight, (in Naigh.

सम्-मद, अस्, आ, अम्, greatly exhilarated, happy,
glad; (अस्), m. exhilaration, happiness, joy, pleasure;
N. of the king of the fish (in Viṣṇu-Purāṇa

); feeling anger or resentment,
angry, fierce, enraged; filled with sorrow, sorrowful;
(उस्), m. epithet of Śiva.

समभिपद् सम्-अभि-पद्, cl. 4. A. -पद्यते,
-पत्तुम्, to come to, arrive at, attain; to come on;
to reply to, answer.

समभिभाष् सम्-अभि-भाष्, cl. 1. A. -भा-
षते, -भाषितुम्, to speak with, converse with;
to speak to, address.

सम्-अभिहार, अस्, m. seizing or taking together;
repetition, reiteration, (क्रिया-समभिहारेण, by a
repetition of acts, by repeated acts); excess, surplus.

समभ्यागा सम्-अभ्य्-आ-गा (-अभि-आ-), cl. 3.
P. -जिगाति, -गातुम्, to come to, come near, approach;
to come upon, assail, attack.

सम्-अर्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, maintained, established;
taken into consideration, considered, judged, regarded,
held; resolved, determined.

2. सम्-अवस्था, f. firm or fixed state or condition;
similar condition or state; state or condition (in
general).

सम्-आकर्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, drawing together;
attracting; spreading or extending far, diffusing
fragrance; (ई), m. a scent spreading afar.

सम्-आगत, अस्, आ, अम्, come together, met,
encountered, joined in close conflict, united, joined;
met together, assembled; being in conjunction (as
the heavenly bodies); come to, approached, arrived;
(आ), f. a kind of riddle or enigma.

सम्-आगम्य, ind. having come together, having
met, having joined in conflict, having gone to meet;
having coalesced; having approached.

),
to sip water (as a religious act forming part of the
ceremony of ablution).

2. सम्-आधा, आस्, m. putting together, adjusting,
settling, reconciling, clearing up difficulties, &c.;
completion, accomplishment.

सम्-आप्लुत, अस्, आ, अम्, bathed, bathing in;
drowned, well drenched, flooded, inundated, over-
whelmed; overflowing or suffused with moisture;
overflowing, filled.

समाभुज् सम्-आ-भुज्, cl. 7. P. A. -भुनक्ति,
-भुङ्क्ते, to enjoy or possess entirely or completely;
to rule over.

समामन्त्र् सम्-आ-मन्त्र्, cl. 10. A. -मन्त्र-
यते, -यितुम्, to address, accost; to invoke, summon;
to bid farewell to any one.

सम्-आयुक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, joined, connected, united;
attached; touched; intent on, devoted to; pre-
pared, made ready; well furnished or endowed with;
supplied, provided; enjoined, charged, appointed;
met together, encountered, brought into contact.

समालुड् सम्-आ-लुड्, Caus. -लोडयति, &c., to
stir or mix together, stir up, agitate, disturb, confuse;
to rummage, investigate.

सम्-आसक्त, अस्, आ, अम्, fastened or joined toge-
ther, attached, united, combined, comprehended;
attached to, fixed on (with loc.); reached, attained;
affected by.

सम्-आस्थाप्य, ind. having caused to be performed;
having duly observed, paying proper regard to; having
placed one's self on a seat, having sat down.
